  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-1523" textLabel="CYP79B2 monooxygenase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-1523" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>CYP79B2 and CYP79B3 are involved in both glucosinolate biosynthesis and auxin biosynthesis. Single mutants have significantly reduced indolic glucosinolates, whereas double mutants have un-detectable indolic glucosinolates and decreased level of IAA |CITS: [12464638]|. Recently, it was shown that double mutants were also devoid of camalexin, suggesting CYP79B2 and CYP79B3 are also involved in camalexin biosynthesis|CITS: [15148388]|. Labeling experiments with indole-3-acetaldoxime confirmed that this intermediate is incorporated into camalexin|CITS: [15148388]|. The induction of CYP79B2 but not CYP79B3 transcripts is closely correlated with camalexin biosynthesis, suggesting CYP79B2 plays an important role in camalexin biosynthesis|CITS: [15148388]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-1523" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP79B2" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT4G39950-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-18601, RXN-18602, RXN-18603, RXN-1825" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="60." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="60." />
